    array.push(cH, "Sunday evening, and the bearish lean on the euro is exactly where the weekend left it.|Sterling waits for Pill, the greenback waits for PCE, and the gap of −7 waits with them.|Tokyo is on holiday tomorrow, so the first chapter of this week will be written in Washington.|A calm Sunday, but the franc's real test is how frightened markets feel at Monday's open.|The widest gap on our board, +14, survives its first quiet evening intact.|The Aussie heads into CPI week still carrying last week's jobs bruise.|The kiwi counts down to Friday's vote count, the dollar counts down to Wednesday's PCE.|Still level at zero, and Sunday gave neither side a reason to move.|Two oil importers, one gap of +1, and a very quiet Sunday.|Neighbours at zero, and the weekend left them that way.|A flat scale at zero, waiting for Wednesday's Australian inflation figure.|Gap +2, two-sided, and no new headline from Paris or Wellington.|Oil remains the hinge, and it did not swing this Sunday evening.|A stand-off at +1, with London speaking first this week and Tokyo on holiday.|Flat at zero after a weekend without news.|Two carry currencies at zero, both waiting for their central banks to speak.|Gap +2, two-sided, and no Sunday surprise for either leg.|The loonie's weakness, not sterling's strength, still carries this +7.|The risk barometer reads +1 and the weekend did not move the needle.|Zero gap, and the carry-versus-haven tug of war paused for Sunday.|The antipodean cousins sit at +2, two-sided, after a quiet Sunday.|The Aussie bruised, the loonie bruised worse: +7 holds into Monday.|Gap −1, two-sided, and the kiwi and yen both stayed silent tonight.|Gap −2, two-sided, and the fear gauge decides more here than any headline.|Milk held, oil spilled, and Sunday changed neither: +5 stays.|Exporter against importer, and the oil gap of −6 is unchanged tonight.|The franc stays favoured at −7 after a newsless Sunday evening.|Two havens at +1, both quiet tonight.|Gold's own score is +1, and the weekend did not change it.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No Fed remark or US data in the hour after the FINAL check; hike path near 92% as logged.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No French budget step, spread print or ECB comment since the FINAL check.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No BoE item since the FINAL check; Pill speaks Monday.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No MoF warning or BoJ comment since the FINAL check; Japan holiday Monday (not verified).|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No SNB item; haven role rests on Friday's VIX 35.9 close.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No oil shock, BoC comment or US–Canada trade step since the FINAL check.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No RBA item or Australian data; October CPI Wednesday.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No RBNZ, dairy or special-vote update since the FINAL check.|CONFIRMED — no new evidence since T0~No ETF, central-bank or real-yield data since the FINAL check; XAU = G +1 + USD +7.")
