    array.push(cH, "Monday's first light finds the euro's bearish lean untouched.|Sterling's day starts at 11:30 with PMIs, the greenback's story hardly moved overnight.|Tokyo is shut for the holiday and the dollar-yen story is unchanged at +8.|The franc's haven story meets a calmer US futures market this morning.|The board's widest gap, +14, opens the week without a scratch.|The Aussie opens the week quietly, with CPI still two days away.|Plot twist in Wellington: retail spending jumped 2.2% in the third quarter.|Two quiet legs and a level scale: EURGBP starts Monday at zero.|Japan takes the day off, and EURJPY stays a near-draw at +1.|Zero gap, and Monday's mixed mood keeps it there.|Still balanced at zero, with Wednesday's CPI the pivot for this pair.|The kiwi just got a shot of good news, and EURNZD's slim tilt narrows.|Oil still leaks lower, and the +7 lean toward the euro holds.|Tokyo is closed, so London writes today's first page at +1.|A flat start to Monday for sterling and the franc.|Two carry currencies at zero, and Monday morning changed nothing.|A strong kiwi retail print nudges this two-sided pair a little closer to even.|The loonie's weakness keeps carrying this +7 into the new week.|The risk barometer opens Monday mixed, and the pair stays at +1.|Carry versus haven, round two: still zero after the Asian open.|The kiwi struck first this week: retail volumes up 2.2% in Q3.|Two bruised commodity currencies, and the loonie is still the more bruised.|A strong retail print for the kiwi while Tokyo takes the day off.|The kiwi's retail surprise trims the franc's slim edge.|Milk, shoppers and cheap oil: this +5 could get even stronger.|Oil stays soft and the −6 lean toward the yen holds.|The franc stays favoured at −7 as markets look for their footing.|Two havens, one holiday, and a gap of +1.|Gold bounced about 2% in Asia, but its score stays at +1.")
